      'The opportunity cost is the value of what was given up, the healthcare improvements. It\'s not the $10 billion (that\'s the explicit cost) but the actual outcomes that won\'t happen: lives that could have been saved, hospitals that won\'t be built. Every allocation decision has an invisible price tag.'
