        'Tool 1: The Federal Funds Rate. This is the Fed\'s primary weapon. By raising this rate, the Fed makes borrowing more expensive throughout the entire economy. Banks pass higher costs to consumers: mortgages, car loans, credit cards, and business loans all get more expensive. Higher borrowing costs mean less spending, less investment, and eventually less inflation. Lowering the rate does the opposite, it stimulates borrowing and spending.',
