        'The 2% target exists because it sits in the sweet spot: high enough to prevent deflation, low enough to preserve purchasing power. At 2%, prices double every 36 years, manageable. At 10%, they double every 7 years. At Zimbabwe levels, they double every day. The difference between 2% and 10% inflation over a 40-year career is the difference between your savings retaining 45% of their value versus just 2%.'
