      'Fighting inflation requires three qualities: (1) Aggressive early action to prevent expectations from becoming unanchored, (2) Independence from political pressure, the Fed must act on data, not popularity, and (3) Patience, monetary policy works with 12-18 month lags, so you must resist the urge to reverse course too early. Paul Volcker\'s painful but successful fight against 1970s inflation remains the gold standard for central banking.'
