      2,
      'Correct! The fiscal multiplier = Total Economic Activity / Government Spending = $160B / $100B = 1.6x. This means every $1 the government spent on infrastructure generated $1.60 in economic output. Infrastructure typically has high multipliers (1.5-2.0x) because it creates construction jobs, improves transportation efficiency, and enables future commerce.',
      'The fiscal multiplier measures bang per buck. Divide total economic activity ($160B) by government spending ($100B) = 1.6x. Infrastructure has one of the highest multipliers because it creates immediate jobs AND long-term productivity gains. By comparison, tax cuts for high earners have multipliers of just 0.3-0.6x because much of the savings is invested or saved rather than spent.'
