            { label: 'Maintain stimulus but announce a clear fiscal plan: spend now, then deficit reduction as the economy recovers', consequence: 'The optimal approach. Continue necessary stimulus while signaling fiscal discipline ahead. This is "counter-cyclical policy": expansionary during downturns, contractionary during recovery. By committing to deficit reduction once unemployment falls below a target (say 5%), you maintain credibility without pulling support too early.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Double the stimulus to accelerate recovery even faster', consequence: 'Risky. The economy is already recovering. Additional stimulus beyond what\'s needed risks overheating and inflation, exactly what happened when COVID stimulus continued into 2021\'s already-recovering economy. More is not always better; the right amount at the right time is the goal.', score: 1 }
