            { label: 'Raise interest rates sharply to attract capital back and make shorting expensive', consequence: 'This is the textbook response. Higher rates attract foreign capital (carry trade inflows), make short-selling the currency expensive, and signal credibility. Mexico used this approach in 2022 (raising rates to 11.25%) and successfully stabilized the peso while other EM currencies fell.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Impose capital controls, ban people from moving money out of the country', consequence: 'Capital controls stop the bleeding but destroy investor confidence permanently. Malaysia imposed them in 1998 and was shut out of international capital markets for years. Investors avoid countries that might trap their money. This is a last resort, not a first move.', score: 0 }
