        'Contrast Nigeria with South Korea (zero oil) and Japan (few natural resources): both became wealthy through manufacturing and human capital. Norway is the rare exception, it avoided the curse by creating a $1.6 trillion sovereign wealth fund that saves oil profits for future generations instead of spending them. Botswana managed diamond wealth successfully through strong institutions. The lesson: resources are a blessing only if institutions are strong enough to manage them.',
        'The Demographic Dividend is a powerful growth accelerator. When birth rates fall (as countries develop), there\'s a "sweet spot" where working-age adults vastly outnumber children and elderly dependents, a large productive workforce supporting fewer dependents. China rode this from 1980-2015, and India is entering it now. India\'s median age is 28 (vs. China\'s 39 and Japan\'s 49), with 900 million people under 45. If India invests in education and job creation for this enormous workforce, it could replicate China\'s growth miracle. If it doesn\'t, it faces mass unemployment and social instability.'
