      'The Fed\'s 2022 rate hikes demonstrate how interconnected the global economy is. Higher U.S. rates strengthened the dollar (DXY hit 114), crushed emerging markets with dollar debt (Sri Lanka defaulted), and eventually cooled commodity prices. Every concept you learned, monetary policy, currencies, trade, development, was involved.'
