      'This is the most common misunderstanding in trade policy. Tariffs are an import tax paid by domestic businesses. Chinese companies receive the same pre-tariff price; American importers pay 25% more, and they pass it to consumers. The Federal Reserve confirmed that tariffs on China cost American households $831/year on average.'
