        { term: 'Deadweight Loss', definition: 'The net economic loss to society from tariffs, the efficiency destroyed by distorting trade patterns away from comparative advantage.', example: 'A USITC study found U.S.-China tariffs caused $3.2 billion in annual deadweight loss, pure economic waste from trade distortion.' }
