        { term: 'Modern Monetary Theory (MMT)', definition: 'The theory that governments issuing their own currency can\'t go bankrupt and should spend freely until inflation constrains them. Taxes serve to manage demand, not fund spending.', example: 'MMT advocates argued the U.S. could fund COVID stimulus without worrying about debt. Critics point to the resulting 9.1% inflation as evidence of MMT\'s risks.' }
