        recap: 'All three camps are arguing over the same 34 trillion, and that number alone cannot settle the argument for any of them. What settles it is r against g. The United States grew out of 106 percent debt after World War Two without repaying much of it, because growth ran ahead of interest, and Greece collapsed at 127 percent because it owed euros it could not print. Lesson 7 handed you deficits as the yearly tool. This is the pile they leave behind, and the interest rate from lesson 3 decides whether that pile quietly shrinks or compounds.',
