      {
        hint: 'Press each of the four blocks to see what job it is actually doing in 2035, and which one you are most likely to be paid in.',
        recap: 'The four blocks are not competing to be money, they have already split the work: CBDCs do the paying, cash fades, Bitcoin sits still, stablecoins carry traffic between the two worlds. So the real contest is not Bitcoin against the dollar, it is over who reads the ledger. China\'s digital yuan matters because it settles trade without touching SWIFT, and lesson 16 showed you exactly what SWIFT access is worth: freezing $300 billion of Russian reserves worked only because the payment rails ran through Washington. Build a second set of rails and that lever gets shorter.',
      }
