        { term: 'Comparative Advantage', definition: 'The principle that countries (and people) should specialize in what they produce at the lowest opportunity cost, then trade for everything else. The foundation of all trade theory.', example: 'Even if the U.S. is better at producing both cars and wheat than Canada, both benefit when each specializes in their lowest opportunity cost product and trades.' }
