            { label: 'Establish a sovereign wealth fund (modeled on Norway), invest in education and healthcare, diversify the economy before extraction begins, and create transparent governance of revenues with independent oversight', consequence: 'This is the Botswana/Norway model. A sovereign wealth fund smooths revenue over decades, avoids Dutch disease, and provides for future generations. Education investment builds human capital. Diversification prevents resource dependency. Transparent governance prevents corruption. You\'ve integrated resource curse theory, development economics, and institutional design.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Sell the extraction rights to international oil companies and use the upfront payment to fund one big project', consequence: 'Selling rights surrenders long-term revenue for short-term cash. International companies will extract most of the value. One big project concentrates risk and invites corruption. This is the DRC model, enormous resources, almost no domestic benefit.', score: 1 }
